    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0212" n="198" xml:id="pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 [Hurley, Patrick J.]: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23T17:00:00+07:00">November 23,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 24—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1890. Political Vice Minister<anchor n="26" xml:id="d179-f1"/> called me to
                    Foreign Office this afternoon and made “oral statement” (of which he handed me
                    text) as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“President Roosevelt was reported to have stated in press conference that
                            he has selected the Ambassador to China and is asking for agreement from
                            China. In the meanwhile newspapers have prominently mentioned Major
                            General Patrick J. Hurley as the likely choice.</p>
                        <p>We have heard nothing officially and therefore desire to enquire
                            informally from the State Department if a decision has been made. For
                            your private information, General Hurley is entirely acceptable to the
                            Chinese Government.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
